1. Licensor and software
   "Software" means the Security Health Check desktop application, the
   security-health-check command-line tool, the bundled collector scripts,
   documentation and all updates provided by s9881 ("Licensor").

2. License grant
   The Licensor grants you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   revocable license to install and use the Software on devices that you
   own or are authorized to administer, for private and commercial
   purposes.

3. Restrictions
   You may not, except where mandatory law expressly permits it:
   a) modify, translate, decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse
      engineer the Software, or create derivative works of it;
   b) sell, rent, lease, sublicense or charge any fee for the Software;
   c) redistribute the Software, except as the unmodified original
      installation packages together with this license, and only free of
      charge;
   d) remove or alter copyright notices, this license or the third-party
      notices;
   e) present the Software, or any part of it, as your own product or as a
      product of anyone other than the Licensor;
   f) use the Software to examine systems you do not own or are not
      authorized to examine.

4. Third-party components
   The Software contains open-source components (for example Flutter, the
   Dart runtime and Dart packages). They are licensed under their own
   licenses, which are shown in the application under "Open Source
   Licenses", printed by "security-health-check licenses --full" and
   included in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Those licenses take precedence for
   the respective components; this agreement does not restrict rights you
   have under them.

5. Use at your own risk; no warranty
   The Software is provided free of charge "AS IS", without warranty of any
   kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and
   accuracy of results. Results are indicators only and may be incomplete or
   wrong. Suggested commands can change system settings, interrupt services
   or remote access, delete data or make a system unbootable; you alone
   decide whether to run them and bear the full risk.

6. Limitation of liability
   To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Licensor is not liable for
   any damage, data loss, downtime, security incident or other consequence
   arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Software. Liability for
   intent and gross negligence, for injury to life, body or health, and
   under mandatory statutory provisions (for example a product liability
   act) remains unaffected.

7. Termination
   This license ends automatically if you breach it. You must then delete
   all copies of the Software.

8. Privacy
   The Software works offline. It does not transmit scan results or
   personal data to the Licensor or third parties. Only actions that you
   start explicitly (for example refreshing package lists) contact the
   update servers configured on your system.

9. Final provisions
   The law of the Federal Republic of Germany applies, excluding the UN
   Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods, unless
   mandatory consumer protection law of your country of residence provides
